# Trained model artifacts — regenerated by backend/ml/train_signal_scorer.py.
#
# Deliberately NOT committed: they are binaries that change on a different
# cadence than code, and every retrain would add another copy to history.
# Because the Docker build context is ./backend, that also means no model is
# ever baked into the image — so the model directory is bind-mounted from the
# host in docker-compose.hetzner.yml instead. Drop a .pkl in
# backend/ml/model_registry/ on the server and restart; no rebuild needed.
#
# This split previously caused a silent failure: a trained model sat in
# backend/ml/model_registry/ locally, was excluded here, never reached the
# container, and production ran heuristic scoring for months while saying so
# only in a startup log line nobody read. /api/health/detail now reports model
# status explicitly so that cannot recur.
backend/ml/model_registry/*.pkl
!backend/ml/model_registry/.gitkeep
